30. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a zone change from A1 - Agricultural
and Rural Residential to CB - Community Business for Tract 2, Winco
Subdivision, and the remaining 1.83-acre parcel situated in the SE1/4
of Sect 20, T14N, R66W, Laramie County, WY.
25 - 240
Section 20, LLC, Zone Change
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services LLC, on behalf of the
landowner, Section 20 LLC, submitted a zone change application for parcels of land
located northwest of E Carlson St and Converse Ave. The purpose of the application
is to change the zone district to one that conforms to the local area and proposed
future development prior to annexation by the city of Cheyenne.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the zone
change from A1 - Agricultural and Rural Residential to CB - Community Business
Tract 2, Winco Subdivision, and the remaining 1.83-acre parcel situated in the
southeast quarter of Sect 20, T14N, R66W, Laramie County, WY, with no conditions.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.
Seth Lloyd, Cheyenne planning, confirmed the pending annexation of the property and
said it's likely the city council would have approved the zone change.  However, he
expressed caution about county approval of zone changes involving property coming
into city limits and said it's best to have city council make those decisions.  He said
future scenarios may not be as optimal or straightforward.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Hollingshead, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to approve a zone change from A-1 – Agricultural
and Rural Residential to CB –Community Business for Tract 2, Winco
Page 9 of 15
