33. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a vacation and administrative plat for
Wyoming Ranchettes, 3rd Filing.
25 - 264
Pave the Way Properties, LLC, Vacation and
Administrative Plat, Wyoming Ranchettes, 3rd Filing
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Jones Land Surveying, Inc, on behalf of Pave the Way
Properties, LLC, submitted an administrative plat application for Wyoming Ranchettes, 3rd
Filing for Lot 1, Block 16, Wyoming Ranchettes, 2nd Filing, Laramie County, WY. The
subject property is located at southeast of the intersection of Crazy Horse and Chief
Twomoon Roads. The purpose of the application is to vacate and divide the 11.73 acre
tract into two residential tracts.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommend approval of the administrative
plat with no conditions and adoption of the findings of fact a, b, and c of the staff report.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.
Residents Ellen Southwell, Maryellen Tast, and Tammy Maas expressed concerns
about traffic, road maintenance, water, increased population density, and impact on
lot sizes.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
Commissioner Zwonitzer said he was not in favor of the proposed plat.  He said he
did not believe splitting the parcels into potentially four additional homes was not
conducive to the neighborhood.
A motion was made by Commissioner Hollingshead, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to approve the administrative plat for Wyoming
Ranchettes, 3rd Filing, with no conditions and adopt the findings of facts
