one condition and adopt the findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
Commissioner Zwonitzer asked the County Attorney if he foresaw any problems with
placing conditions on Rd 210 the future.  Brad Lund, deputy county attorney, said their
office drafted a proposed condition to address concerns about road improvements.
He read the proposed condition into the record. Molly Bennett, Public Works, said she
felt the condition was appropriate.  She noted that Happy Jack Rd is under the
jurisdiction of WY Dept of Transportation and Rd 210 is a county road.
A motion was made by Commissioner Heath, seconded by Commissioner
Zwonitzer, to amend the motion to add the following condition as read by
the County Attorney:  Approval of a road use and maintenance agreement
between applicant and County, to the satisfaction of, Laramie County
Public Works, to address the impact of the applicant's mining operations
and use of all existing and anticipated roads: a) on the site, and b) County
roads leading to the site.
 The motion carried by the following vote:
